# 🧬 LeadGen → CRM Integration Architecture (Full Context)

> This section maps the external lead-generation pipeline (ClinicalTrials.gov, NIH, ASCO) into first-class CRM entities, jobs, dashboards, and outreach sequences – fully inside our app.

## A) Data Model (DocTypes)

- `LeadGen Source` (Single)
  - Fields: `clinicaltrials_api_key?`, `nih_reporter_endpoint`, `asco_source_url`, `default_country`, `max_page_size`, `rate_limits`, `last_run_at`
  - Purpose: Central configuration for all lead-gen collectors

- `LeadGen Job`
  - Fields: `job_type (Enum: trials|nih|asco|consolidate)`, `status (Queued|Running|Completed|Failed)`, `params (JSON)`, `started_at`, `ended_at`, `log (Long Text)`, `result_file (File)`
  - Purpose: Track fetch/enrich/consolidate runs; surfaced in SPA dashboard

- `Lead Prospect`
  - Fields: `pi_name`, `pi_email`, `institution`, `phone`, `source (Enum: trials|nih|asco|manual)`, `source_ref_id (NCT ID / Grant ID / Abstract ID)`, `cancer_type`, `endpoint_summary`, `funding_total`, `h_index`, `recent_papers`, `lead_score (Int)`, `tier (Data)`, `raw (JSON)`
  - Purpose: Staging area before promoting to core CRM entities

- `Lead Prospect Match`
  - Fields: `prospect (Link Lead Prospect)`, `matched_doctype (Enum: Contact|CRM Lead|CRM Organization)`, `matched_name`, `confidence (0-1)`, `strategy (email|name+institution|domain)`
  - Purpose: Entity resolution audit trail and manual review

- Reuse core CRM DocTypes
  - `CRM Organization`, `Contact`, `CRM Lead` (add custom fields: `h_index`, `lead_source`, `tier`, `lead_score`, `prospect_ref`)

- `Outreach Sequence` / `Outreach Step`
  - Sequence fields: `name`, `audience_filter (JSON)`, `channel (email|call)`, `status`, `owner`
  - Step fields: `sequence (Link)`, `offset_days`, `template_ref`, `conditions (JSON)`, `active`
  - Purpose: Declarative follow-up programs (Day 0, 3, 7, 14)

## B) ETL + Jobs (Collectors inside CRM)

- Files
  - `crm/leadgen/clinicaltrials_collector.py` (port scripts → Frappe jobs)
  - `crm/leadgen/nih_collector.py`
  - `crm/leadgen/asco_collector.py`
  - `crm/leadgen/consolidate.py` (dedupe, score, tier)

- Whitelisted APIs
  - `crm.api.leadgen.run_job(job_type: str, params: dict)` → enqueue specific collector
  - `crm.api.leadgen.job_status(job_name)` → status/logs/links
  - `crm.api.leadgen.promote_prospects(prospect_names: list[str])` → upsert Organization/Contact/CRM Lead with links

- Schedulers (hooks)
  - `scheduler_events.daily`: optional nightly refresh (guarded by flags)

## C) Scoring, Tiering, and Promotion

- Scoring function
  - `score = min(h_index, 50) + 2*recent_papers + 30*(has_active_trial) + 20*(has_asco) + min(total_funding/1e6, 30)`
  - Implemented in `crm/leadgen/consolidate.py` and stored on `Lead Prospect.lead_score`

- Tiering
  - Tier 1 (≥100), Tier 2 (50–99), Tier 3 (<50) → stored; visible in list filters

- Promotion pipeline
  - Attempt entity resolution (Contact by email > Org by domain > fallback Lead)
  - Create/Link: `CRM Organization` (by institution/domain), `Contact` (PI), `CRM Lead` (if new initiative)
  - Write a `FCRM Note` summarizing source evidence (trials/grants/abstracts)

## D) Outreach Sequences (Inside CRM)

- Email
  - Templates stay in repo (Jinja) or `Email Template` DocType
  - Rendering endpoint: `crm.api.outreach.render_template(template_id, context)`
  - Draft creation: `crm.api.email.save_draft_with_provider` + store draft to Communication
  - Sequence runner: `crm/api/outreach.py` → expands audience (Lead/Contact filters) → schedules steps as `ToDo` or drafts

- Follow-ups
  - Job `crm.api.outreach.apply_sequences()` daily: check sent_at, compute day offsets, create next draft or ToDo

- Tracking
  - Replies captured via inbound `Communication` hook; update `reply_status` custom field on linked Lead/Contact; dashboard metrics

## E) SPA: LeadGen Dashboard

- Route: `/crm/leadgen` → `frontend/src/pages/LeadGenDashboard.vue`
  - Widgets: Jobs by status, Prospects by tier, Promotions pending, Outreach progress
  - Actions: Run job (trial/nih/asco/consolidate), Promote selected Prospects, Start sequence, Export CSV
  - Data sources: `crm.api.leadgen.job_status`, `frappe.get_list('Lead Prospect', ...)`, `crm.api.outreach.get_sequences()`

## F) Intelligence + Farfalle (Contextual Assistance)

- In Prospect view / Lead form
  - Button: "Analyze PI" → calls Farfalle `/intel/enrich_lead` with institution/domain → returns key themes; save as `FCRM Note`
- In sequence authoring
  - Button: "AI Draft" for a cohort → Farfalle suggests subject/body variants; user picks; posts drafts via `email.save_draft`

## G) Permissions, Privacy, Compliance

- Row-level
  - Sales Users: If Owner semantics on `CRM Lead` and `Lead Prospect` (owner set to creator/assignee)
  - Managers: full read/write

- PII handling
  - Prospect raw JSON stored in `Lead Prospect.raw`; `FCRM Note` content kept concise; transcripts (voice) default private (owner+manager)

- Compliance
  - Add unsubscribe/footer macros into templates (CAN-SPAM); configurable sender accounts

## H) Observability and Self-Improvement Loop

- Logs and Metrics
  - `LeadGen Job` tracks timings, counts, failures; daily aggregates; simple `crm/public/frontend` dashboard widgets

- A/B Testing
  - Template variants tracked by `template_ref`; store reply/meeting outcomes; weekly summary; recommend winning variants

- Feedback → Model
  - On reply categorized as Interested/Maybe/Not: update prospect features; adjust weightings; write back recommended tier shifts

## I) Deployment & Ops

- Configurable via `LeadGen Source` (rate limits, endpoints)
- Jobs enqueue-safe; backoff on API errors; resumable via `result_file` artifacts
- Staging-first: run collectors on staging site with throttled settings; promote after verification

## J) End-to-End Example

1) Run Trials + NIH + ASCO collectors from `/crm/leadgen` → `LeadGen Job`s populate `Lead Prospect`
2) Consolidate job → scores + tiers; unresolved matches flagged in `Lead Prospect Match`
3) Promote Tier 1 → create/link Org/Contact/Lead → attach `FCRM Note` with evidence
4) Start "Tier 1 Sequence" → Day 0 draft emails created; user reviews and sends
5) Inbound replies auto-link to Lead/Contact; dashboard updates; next steps scheduled automatically

